<Base title="Privacy" description="How this blog handles browser preferences, hosting, and analytics.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-10">
    <div class="serif space-y-5 text-foreground leading-relaxed">
<h1 class="display text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Summary</h1>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated November 11, 2026.</p>
<p>We respect your privacy. Your preferences are stored locally in your browser using a first-party theme cookie. This means your preferences do not sync between devices. We do not track you across websites, and we do not collect names or email addresses through our analytics.</p>
<p>This website is hosted on Cloudflare Workers, which may process limited technical data for security and performance. We also use self-hosted Umami to collect aggregated usage statistics to help improve the website. For more information on how these services handle data, refer to their respective privacy policies.</p>

<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Data we collect</h2>
<p>This website does not use tracking cookies. Your theme preference is stored locally in your browser using a first-party theme cookie. We do not send names, email addresses, or form contents to Umami. However, we use a script provided by Umami for usage statistics.</p>
<p>If you submit a comment where comments are enabled, the blog stores your name, email address, and comment. Published comments show your name and comment text. This is separate from analytics.</p>

<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Cloudflare Workers</h2>
<p>We use Cloudflare Workers provided by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA ("Cloudflare") as our hosting provider. Using Cloudflare Workers allows us to provide a stable and secure website.</p>
<p>As a hosting provider, Cloudflare may process the following information:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
<li>IP addresses</li>
<li>Referring websites</li>
<li>Date and time</li>
<li>Data volume</li>
<li>Website addresses</li>
<li>Browser and operating system information</li>
</ul>
<p>Cloudflare may aggregate usage data for statistical and operational purposes. More detailed information is available at <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" class="acid-link">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Umami Software</h2>
<p>We use Umami, a privacy-friendly web analytics service hosted by us, to collect data about website usage. This helps us understand overall traffic trends, such as which pages are visited most.</p>
<p>The data collected by Umami includes:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
<li>Page views and page addresses</li>
<li>Referring URLs</li>
<li>Device type, browser, operating system, language, and screen size</li>
<li>IP addresses, processed to derive location and visitor statistics</li>
<li>Approximate location</li>
<li>Time of visit and duration</li>
</ul>
<p>Umami does not use tracking cookies and does not store raw IP addresses in analytics records. It uses a rotating hashed identifier to group visits. We do not supply personal user IDs or use session recordings. The tracker respects your browser’s Do Not Track setting.</p>
<p>You can read more about <a href="https://docs.umami.is/docs/faq" class="acid-link">Umami’s privacy practices</a>.</p>

<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
<p>If you have any questions about this privacy policy or the data we process, you can reach us at: <a href="mailto:therealsamyak@gmail.com" class="acid-link">therealsamyak@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
